<?php

/**
 * What this plugin uses, and how each is configured.
 *
 * `wp zt add module <name>` appends to this file, so a module works as soon as
 * it is copied. The entry file reads it with `$plugin->bootstrap()`.
 *
 * An entry is a class name on its own, or a class name with a configuration
 * array:
 *
 * ```
 * Cron::class,                    // no configuration
 * Cron::class => array(           // configured
 *     'configure' => function ( Cron $cron ): void {
 *         $cron->add_custom_interval( 'every_15_minutes', 900, 'Every 15 Minutes' );
 *     },
 * ),
 * ```
 *
 * The array takes three keys, all optional:
 *
 * - `configure` -- runs when the module is first built, before it boots. The
 *   place to call whatever setters it offers.
 * - `boots_on` -- a WordPress hook to boot on, for a module that cannot do its
 *   work as the plugin loads. Without it the module boots as `run()` reaches it.
 * - `priority` -- what `boots_on` binds at. Defaults to 10.
 *
 * Everything works without an array, so add one only to change a default. See a
 * module's own page for what it accepts.
 *
 * This file is modules only, and listing one is what builds it. A module acts
 * on its own -- it binds a hook, registers a post type, walks a directory -- so
 * it has to be built for any of that to happen. Leave one out and its
 * `on_boot()` never runs, with no error to say so; `wp zt doctor` catches that.
 *
 * A service does not belong here. It is built the moment something asks for it
 * -- a `$plugin->get()`, or another class declaring a property of its type --
 * so listing it would only build it sooner than it needed to be. One that takes
 * configuration gets it from `$plugin->configure()` in your entry file.
 *
 * An entry file that runs the plugin as it loads runs `configure` before
 * `init`, where a `__()` loads the text domain early enough that WordPress
 * reports `_load_textdomain_just_in_time` on every request. Naming a `boots_on`
 * moves the whole module past that point:
 *
 * ```
 * Blocks::class => array(
 *     'boots_on'    => 'init',
 *     'configure' => function ( Blocks $blocks ): void {
 *         $blocks->add_categories( array( 'reports' => __( 'Reports', '{{text_domain}}' ) ) );
 *     },
 * ),
 * ```
 */

declare( strict_types=1 );

// Loaded by the plugin, never requested directly.
\defined( 'ABSPATH' ) || exit;

return array();
